WEBVTT

00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:25,000
I have breast cancer, should I do surgery in chemo as they ask me to do? Well, like I tell even our patients, you have to make that decision, that's not our decision, whether you do surgery in chemo as they ask you to do, regardless of what you decide to do with standards of care, that their appropriate or inappropriate for every person is different.

00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:47,000
So, I'm not against chemo and surgery and radiation at all, and I think it's very appropriate for a lot of people, but I am against anybody just jumping down a course of care because they, A, I think it's sad if they think that they have no other option, and B, that they are making that decision completely based upon fear.

00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:04,000
So, that tends to be the case scenario, most people are here that they have cancer, their sympathetic nervous system goes into a state of fight or flight, and it's very hard for them to make any rational decision, and they can just hurt it down a pathway that they later regret.

00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:18,000
So, just slow down, it's my first piece of advice, slow down, go to prayer, make sure that you have peace that literally passes all understated about what you're doing, and that you know that you're going to be taking care of through that.

00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:30,000
And regardless, so whether you decide to do standards of care, that you're going to be better off if you add some alternative things as well, it will increase your survival statistics even more.

00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:39,000
So, so the more alternative things that you could do, the better off I think you will be, whether you do standards of care or not.

